cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use any part of this work (code, ideas, mathematical formulations or findings), please cite it as below."
title: "Ternary State-Space Models: Hardware-Efficient Language Modeling with Custom C/Vulkan Training"
authors:
  - family-names: Lena
    given-names: Julio Jose
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/alucardeht/ternary-ssm"
url: "https://github.com/alucardeht/ternary-ssm"
license: MIT
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
abstract: >-
  Transformer alternatives on minimal hardware. A ternary {-1, 0, +1}
  state-space language model with a handwritten C/Vulkan training pipeline
  (no PyTorch, no CUDA) whose Forward Programming fits 3.38B parameters in
  893 MB of VRAM, and BSR, a brain-inspired model with no trained network
  that learns language by counting and stores each fact in one memory write.
keywords:
  - transformer alternative
  - state-space models
  - ternary neural networks
  - matmul-free
  - efficient language models
  - Vulkan
  - gradient-free learning
  - one-shot learning
  - continual learning
  - brain-inspired computing
